  "question": {
    "text": "The bob of a pendulum is released from a horizontal position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> as shown in the figure. If the length of the pendulum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, what is the speed with which the bob arrives at the lowermost point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, given that it dissipated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of its initial energy against air resistance?<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/mmyeuubnnwyrdvcrrgikcqevpbtsnwyeddvxxrgrrlyfepcajz.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YOIOb",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><div id=\"gtx-trans\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 47px; top: -8px;\"><div class=\"gtx-trans-icon\">&nbsp;</div></div>",
